DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzffiillee is the file manager of the COHERENT GUI.  It must be
     run under the zzvviieeww desktop.  It shows one directory at a
     time in `ls -l' style - mode string, name (directories with
     a trailing /), size and date - with directories sorted
     first, then files, alphabetically.  A button bar offers
     EEddiitt, CCooppyy, MMoovvee, DDeelleettee, MMkkddiirr and GGoo, and a path line
     shows the current directory.

     The _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y argument must be an absolute path (starting
     with /); without one, zzffiillee starts at the root.  zzffiillee also
     accepts the standard window _o_p_t_i_o_n_s of GUI applications; see
     zzvviieeww.

     Keyboard commands (the cursor keypad maps onto the control
     keys as usual):

                ^PP, ^NN          select the previous / next entry
                ^ZZ, ^BB          page the list up
                ^VV, ^FF, SSPPAACCEE   page the list down
                ^AA, CCLLRR/HHOOMMEE    select the first entry
                ^EE              select the last entry
                RREETTUURRNN          enter the selected directory
                BBSS              go to the parent directory
                HHEELLPP            show the help summary
                ee, FF22           Edit: open the selected file in zedit
                cc, FF33           Copy the selected file
                mm, FF44           Move (or rename) the selected file
                dd, FF55           Delete the selected file or empty directory
                kk, FF66           Mkdir: create a directory
                gg, FF77           Go to a typed absolute path

     A left click selects an entry; clicking the selected entry
     again within a second enters it if it is a directory.  The
     scrollbar on the left edge scrolls the list.

     The operations ask for names and confirmations in dialogs
     (RETURN fires the default button, ESC cancels, TAB moves be-
     tween fields).  Their semantics:

     CCooppyy copies an ordinary file, in zzffiillee itself; a destination
          that is an existing directory receives the file under
          its own name, and overwriting an existing file is con-
          firmed.

     MMoovvee links and unlinks, so it works within one file system
          only and refuses directories.  A move within the same
          directory is how a file is renamed.



